{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqq52ygnlmd","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"onboard-code sync must read lastIndexedCommit from the daemon, not assume none","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: the incremental git-diff sync (lib/code-extract/sync.js syncRepo) persists lastIndexedCommit via POST /config but a fresh CLI --sync invocation has NO in-process memory of it, so it MUST read the watermark back from the daemon before diffing. Observed live in the E2E: without a daemon read, syncRepo found no watermark, returned full_onboard_needed, and the CLI fell back to a FULL onboard — which only ADDS symbols and never removes the deleted file's code_nodes, so a deleted file's symbols lingered in retrieval. Fix: added GET /config (routes/session.js) + httpDaemonClient.getLastIndexedCommit (sync.js), and syncRepo resolves the watermark in order: explicit lastCommit > injected opts.getLastIndexedCommit > client.getLastIndexedCommit (the daemon read the CLI relies on). The watermark is keyed by the repo ABS path. Lesson for any future code-sync caller: the watermark lives in the daemon's overlay.config.lastIndexedCommit[repoAbs], not in the CLI process.","category":"project","tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-23T04:23:27.479Z","vec":[-0.10895708948373795,-0.0028457590378820896,0.03690704330801964,0.02290290966629982,0.11979895830154419,-0.0729304775595665,0.03017650917172432,-0.008230720646679401,0.06920244544744492,0.03477988764643669,0.04555325582623482,0.0592787079513073,0.005685629788786173,-0.0333048515021801,-0.04816344380378723,-0.02712041512131691,-0.020820561796426773,-0.02802676521241665,-0.037489693611860275,-0.0036865570582449436,-0.04227365925908089,-0.025547578930854797,-0.0015592265408486128,0.047832902520895004,0.009122412651777267,0.07045171409845352,-0.045797791332006454,-0.01824657805263996,-0.027308311313390732,0.0077364821918308735,0.05043556168675423,0.030078977346420288,-0.05273497477173805,-0.013828101567924023,-0.0018828138709068298,0.1